<div class="instructions locations">
  <p>The location indicates the place where the experiment was conducted and the data was collected. <strong>For multiple locations (e.g. multiple fields) use the "Add More" button to add a form element for each one.</strong></p>

  <dl>
    <dt>Field</dt>
      <dd> Include the name of the closest town/landmark, province, country and optionally the geographical coordinates of each site (e.g. "Sutherland, SK, Canada").</dd>
    <dt>Greenhouse</dt>
      <dd>Include the name of the closest town/landmark, province, country and optionally the geographical coordinates of each greenhouse (e.g. "Sutherland, SK, Canada").</dd>
    <dt>Growth Chamber</dt>
      <dd>Include the unique identifier, name of the facility, province, country and optionally the geographical coordinates of each growth chamber (e.g. "A5, USASK Phytotron, SK, Canada").</dd>
    <dt>Biochemical Assay</dt>
      <dd>Provide the laboratory that this experiment took place in. Include the company name or university, room number and building name, and city and province (e.g. 1A23, Agriculture Building, USASK, Saskatoon, SK).</dd>
  </dl>
</div>
